From: fish <lunarisfelix02@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] op7t-0169: Bluetooth, step 2: the UART up, the WCN3990 asked its version

0168 showed (2026-11-10): SE3 of QUP wrapper 2 runs once voted, from the
19.2 MHz XO (its RCG has no DFS table), with the UART protocol firmware
(rev 0x20b) loaded; gpio43..46 still in their gpio/sleep state.

`sysctl kern.sweetbt=1` now (root, once):
- sets SE3's RCG to 7.3728 MHz (GPLL0_OUT_EVEN * 384/15625, as Linux
  gcc-sm8150): 115200 baud = divider 2, 2400 = 96 at 32x oversampling
  (16x if QUP_HW_VER >= 2.5, read from the wrapper);
- muxes gpio43..46 to qup13 with the DT "active" pulls;
- sets the SE up as Linux qcom_geni_serial (FIFO mode, packing 4x8 lsb
  first, 8N1, RX stale 160 bits), polled;
- puts the WCN3990 in boot mode as Linux hci_qca: power-off pulse 0xC0
  at 2400 baud, power-on pulse 0xFC at 115200 (flow control off, RTS
  held), 100 ms, then RTS/CTS on and RX started;
- sends EDL get version (01 00 fc 01 19; expects vendor event 04 ff ..
  00 02 + product, patch, ROM, SoC id) and HCI_Reset (01 03 0c 00),
  logs every byte that comes back, decodes the ROM version into the
  firmware names (image/crbtfwXX.tlv, image/crnvXX.bin).
No firmware sent yet. kern.sweetbt reads 1 clock, 2 UART up, 3 version
answered, 4 reset answered; -1/-2/-3 stopped (clock, mapping, not UART).
Stub-compiled with clang -Wall -Wextra -Wshorten-64-to-32.

Apply after 0168.
